 <hola@pablodorado.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 14:24:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] build(precompile): the current VOS precompile shim for
 pvm-precompile

pvm-precompile pinned zkpvm-precompiles at VOS 9f5337f, whose shim emits a
bare ecall that today's PVM compiler translates into a trap: the first
curve operation of a guest built with the feature panicked. It now uses
vos-pvm-precompiles, the current shim, which marks its ECALLs (csrw 0x801)
and keeps the same API. Agent runtimes serve 110-114 (VOS fork branch
agent/execution-limits, natively with the runtime feature native-curve).
vos-protocol moves to the same VOS revision.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
